# Managed by the playground capture Ansible role.
#
# Ubuntu's /etc/apparmor.d/usr.sbin.tcpdump confines where tcpdump may
# write. NOTE this is NOT the reason a fresh guest's capture works --
# measured live on Noble with that profile in enforce mode, the STOCK
# profile (no override of ours in place) already permits `**.pcap*`
# writes anywhere on the filesystem: `.pcap`, `.pcap0`, `.pcap00`, and
# `.pcap39` all wrote successfully to an arbitrary directory outside
# this grant, while a `.dat` file in the same directory was denied with
# "Permission denied". `-Z root` (see capture-start.j2) is the setting
# that actually gates whether a write into {{ capture_dir }} succeeds at
# all; this file is defence-in-depth against a FUTURE filename that
# doesn't match `**.pcap*`, not the thing standing between a fresh guest
# and a working capture today. The shipped profile ends with
# `#include <local/usr.sbin.tcpdump>`, so widening it here is still the
# supported route if that ever changes -- do not disable confinement
# instead.
#
# capture_dir defaults to /var/lib/playground/capture/ (see
# ansible/roles/capture/defaults/main.yml); the grant below tracks
# whatever value is actually configured.
{{ capture_dir }}/ rw,
{{ capture_dir }}/** rw,
